<section class="why shell" id="why">
  <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal><span>01</span>Why</p>
  <p class="why-statement" data-reveal>
    Writing code is no longer the slow part. A team with coding agents can ship in a week what used
    to take a quarter.
    <span class="mute"
      >That is great news for most software. For software that has to be right, it is a problem.</span
    >
  </p>
  <div class="why-cols">
    <p data-reveal>
      Think of a tax calculation, a loan decision, an identity check, or a record you may have to
      show a regulator. There, &ldquo;it looks like it works&rdquo; is not good enough. An agent
      that is confidently wrong is worse than no agent at all.
    </p>
    <p data-reveal>
      Most regulated companies either ban the tools and fall behind, or let everyone experiment and
      hope nothing breaks. Neither holds up once GDPR, the EU&nbsp;AI&nbsp;Act or an auditor asks
      how a result was produced.
    </p>
    <p data-reveal class="why-close">
      There is a better path. Treat the rules as part of the system, make every step checkable, and
      let AI do the fast part. <strong>That is what Ast does.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
